The intended future presentation order is authoritative/civil presentation
time → physical 12-hour formatting → active-font width measurement →
centered target layout → optional transition/recenter presentation behavior →
overlays/effects → logical framebuffer → brightness/output processing →
display transport. Effects and special-day behavior are presentation policy;
they do not own formatting or authoritative time. If a new string changes the
centered target origin, presentation may subtly animate from the prior logical
position to the new one (for example, `9:59`→`10:00` or `12:59`→`1:00`).
Animation is relevant only when the target origin changes; no shift or wobble
is required when it stays the same. The new time value becomes the
presentation's current value immediately; animation may affect only its visual
placement and must not hold back the update. Authoritative time never waits
